NEW FILE LibKa0s/OptionsKeybinds.lua (CRLF; ASCII strings, em dash as "\226\128\148", arrows as "->"), the OptionsDrawer.lua:1-40 shape:
- Header comment: what it is (the settings-panel editor for a host's launcher-§6 bindings), why a library surface though launcher-§6's recorded rejection (LibKa0s#58) stands for Bindings.xml and the BINDING_* globals (this file writes NO BINDING_* global, reads Bindings.xml never, sets no default key), the b902e35 supersession, the rules it keeps (never touches SettingsPanel, KeybindListener, Settings.*BindingSet*, HideUIPanel, ToggleGameMenu; no SetPropagateKeyboardInput; never reuses KeyBindingFrameBindingTemplate or AceGUI's Keybinding widget — reasons from §5.1: Escape clears there, no META, BUTTON5 cap, English-only message, FULLSCREEN_DIALOG level-1000 toplevel msgframe).
- `local lib = LibStub and LibStub("LibKa0s-Options-1.0", true)`; `local core = LibStub and LibStub("LibKa0s-Core-1.0", true)`; `local KEYBINDS_MINOR = 1`; paired guard exactly as OptionsDrawer.lua:33-36 with `lib.__keybindsMinor` / `lib.__keybindsShellMinor`; `lib.MODULES.OptionsKeybinds = KEYBINDS_MINOR`.
- Strings: `lib.KEYBIND_STRINGS` (library-level literal table, the OptionsIds.lua:185-196 ID_TEXT pattern; a host overrides any key through `spec.strings` in LK-12). Keys and default text: TAB_LABEL "Keybindings"; TAB_TIP "The same key bindings as Options -> Keybindings. A key set here shows there, and the other way round."; INTRO "Key bindings are saved by the game, not in your profile. Defaults and Reset all settings leave them alone." (XC-02, verbatim); UNCHANGED "Key bindings are not changed." (XC-02's Defaults-tooltip tail); KEY1 "Key 1"; KEY2 "Key 2"; CLEAR "Clear"; CLEAR_TIP "Remove both keys from this action."; SLOT_TIP "Click, then press a key or a mouse button to bind it. Esc cancels. Right-click removes this key."; LISTENING "Press a key..."; SET_ACCOUNT "Saved for all characters."; SET_CHARACTER "Saved for this character only."; SET_HOW "Change this with Options -> Keybindings -> Character Specific Keybindings."; COMBAT "Key bindings can be changed after combat."; FAILED "That key could not be bound."; CLEARED "Key removed."; UNAVAILABLE "Key bindings cannot be set here on this client. Use Options -> Keybindings.". The client's own strings win where they exist, read at use: NOT_BOUND (fallback "Not bound"), KEY_BOUND (fallback "Key bound."), KEY_UNBOUND_ERROR (fallback "%s is now unbound.").
- The chord builder, file-local and exposed for the suite as `lib.__keyChord(key, mods)`: returns nil for an ignored press (meta keys alone LSHIFT RSHIFT LCTRL RCTRL LALT RALT LMETA RMETA, UNKNOWN, BUTTON1, BUTTON2, and ESCAPE which cancels), else the chord with prefixes ALT- CTRL- SHIFT- META- in that order. Mouse names convert first: LeftButton BUTTON1, RightButton BUTTON2, MiddleButton BUTTON3, Button4..Button31 BUTTON4..BUTTON31; the wheel arrives as MOUSEWHEELUP / MOUSEWHEELDOWN. Client route first, guarded: `GetConvertedKeyOrButton`, `IsKeyPressIgnoredForBinding`, `CreateKeyChordStringUsingMetaKeyState` when each is a function; otherwise the bundled copy reading IsAltKeyDown / IsControlKeyDown / IsShiftKeyDown / IsMetaKeyDown (each guarded; `mods` overrides for the suite). PRINTSCREEN is not bound: the capture (LK-12) calls `Screenshot()` when it exists, as Blizzard does (BindingUtil.lua:82-86).
- `lib.__keybindAvailable()` -> true when GetBindingKey, GetBindingAction, SetBinding, SaveBindings and GetCurrentBindingSet are all functions.
- `lib.__keybindSet(command, slot, key)` -> `ok, displaced, displacedUnbound, reason` (pure apart from the client API; no frames): (1) refuse with reason "combat" when `lib.__IsCombatLocked()` (Options.lua:367), calling no binding API; (2) reason "unavailable" when not available; (3) `k1, k2 = GetBindingKey(command)`; if key equals the key already in `slot`, return true (no write, no save); (4) `old = GetBindingAction(key)`, `displaced = (old ~= "" and old ~= command) and old or nil`; (5) unbind the command's keys (`SetBinding(k, nil)` for k1, k2); (6) if displaced, `SetBinding(key, nil)`; (7) build the new order: the old keys minus `key`, with `key` placed at `slot` (slot 2 on a command with no other key becomes slot 1), and rebind in order with `SetBinding(k, command)` (Blizzard's RebindKeysInOrder, Blizzard_Keybindings.lua:103-110, :176-188); (8) if any rebind returns falsy: unbind what was bound, rebind k1 then k2 to command, rebind `key` to `displaced` when there was one, and return false, nil, nil, "failed" with NO SaveBindings; (9) `displacedUnbound = displaced ~= nil and GetBindingKey(displaced) == nil`; (10) `SaveBindings(GetCurrentBindingSet())` once; (11) return true, displaced, displacedUnbound.
- `lib.__keybindClear(command, slot)` -> `ok, reason`: same refusals; slot nil clears both keys; slot 1/2 unbinds only that slot's key (the other keeps its place); a command with nothing to clear returns true with no save; otherwise one SaveBindings(GetCurrentBindingSet()).
- `lib.__keybindSetName()` -> "character" when `GetCurrentBindingSet()` equals `(Enum and Enum.BindingSet and Enum.BindingSet.Character) or CHARACTER_BINDINGS or 2`, else "account".
- `function lib.__AttachKeybinds(O, d)` exists but attaches no public member yet (LK-12 adds them); keep it a no-op body with a comment.
- Every function CCN <= 15 (automated-tests-§3 release gate); split helpers as needed.

