FILE LibKa0s/OptionsKeybinds.lua: KEYBINDS_MINOR 1 -> 2 (`Minor 2:` note). `lib.__AttachKeybinds(O, d)` now defines three instance members:
1. `O.KEYBINDS_UNCHANGED = lib.KEYBIND_STRINGS.UNCHANGED` — the sentence a host appends to its General page's Defaults tooltip (XC-02).
2. `O.KeybindingsTab(spec)` -> a host-tab entry for `O.RenderTabbedSchema`'s `opts.tabs` (OptionsTabs.lua:1294-1297, render(ctx, rows) pcall'd at :1246): `{ key = spec.key or "Keybindings", label = spec.label or S.TAB_LABEL, tooltip = spec.tooltip or S.TAB_TIP, before = spec.before, render = function(ctx) O.KeybindRows(ctx, spec) end }`. spec: `bindings` (array of `{ command = "CLICK X:LeftButton", tooltip = optional string }`, order = row order; the host's NS.BINDINGS, which its tests compare with Bindings.xml through T.assertBindingsXml), `key`, `label`, `tooltip`, `before` (nil = last, XC-01), `intro` (string to replace the default, or false to draw none; default S.INTRO), `note` (optional extra line after the intro: QuickComms' 'a dial's key follows its place in the dial list'), `strings` (overrides of lib.KEYBIND_STRINGS keys). A hand-drawn strip (LootHistory's GENERAL_TABS, settings/Panel.lua:956-1035) uses `{ key = "Keybindings", build = function(ctx) O.KeybindRows(ctx, SPEC) end }`.
3. `O.KeybindRows(ctx, spec, parent)` -> array of row records (for tests) or nil when degraded. parent defaults to `O.EnsureScroll(ctx)`; with no AceGUI or scroll it returns nil having drawn nothing.
   - Degradation: when `not lib.__keybindAvailable()`, draw one `O.TextRow(ctx, S.UNAVAILABLE)` and return nil.
   - Intro (unless false) and note: `O.TextRow` lines, then a spacer (`O.AddSpacer(scroll, O.ROW_VSPACER)`).
   - One row per binding, an AceGUI SimpleGroup (Flow, full width) holding: a Label with `GetBindingName(command)` (fallback `_G["BINDING_NAME_"..command]` or the command; NO label is passed in, so the two pages cannot drift), relative width 0.40; slot buttons Key 1 and Key 2 (AceGUI Button, 0.22 each) showing `GetBindingText(key)` (fallback the key) or NOT_BOUND; a Clear button (0.12). Widths sum below 1 (options-ui-§8's clip inset). Tooltips through `O.AttachTooltip`: the row's spec tooltip on the label, S.SLOT_TIP on slots, S.CLEAR_TIP on Clear. A row whose command is not a string is skipped and reported with `lib.STRINGS.ROW_FAILED`.
   - Below the rows two Labels: the set line `S.SET_ACCOUNT` or `S.SET_CHARACTER` (from lib.__keybindSetName) followed by ' ' .. S.SET_HOW, and the status line (empty until an action).
   - Disabled page (`ctx.__renderDisabled`, OptionsTabs.lua:1240-1249): slots and Clear are SetDisabled(true).
   - Each row pushes a refresher into `ctx.refreshers` that repaints its two slots and the set line from GetBindingKey (no key is cached anywhere; a repaint always re-reads).
   - Slot clicks: the slot's frame is `RegisterForClicks("LeftButtonUp", "RightButtonUp")` (restored to "LeftButtonUp" in the widget's OnRelease callback, so a pooled Button leaves with nothing of ours: options-ui-§19). OnClick(button): RightButton -> `O.__combatRefused("keybind", command)` then `lib.__keybindClear(command, slot)`, status S.CLEARED; LeftButton -> start capture on this slot (a second LeftButton while listening on it cancels). Clear -> `lib.__keybindClear(command, nil)`.
   - Capture: ONE library-level listener frame `lib.__keybindListener` (created once, kept across a LibStub upgrade like lib.__parkFrame; a plain Frame that draws nothing — frame-layering T0, no strata or level of its own). Start (refused through `O.__combatRefused("keybind", command)` in combat, status S.COMBAT): stop any other capture; SetParent the listener to the slot button's frame, SetAllPoints it, `EnableKeyboard(true)`, `EnableMouse(true)`, `EnableMouseWheel(true)`, Show; the slot text reads S.LISTENING. OnKeyDown(key): ESCAPE cancels (Escape never reaches the settings window because the keyboard-enabled frame consumes it; never call SetPropagateKeyboardInput); PRINTSCREEN calls Screenshot() if present and keeps listening; otherwise `chord = lib.__keyChord(key)`, nil keeps listening, else write. OnMouseDown(button): LeftButton or RightButton cancel (click again to cancel); other buttons convert through __keyChord and write. OnMouseWheel(delta): MOUSEWHEELUP / MOUSEWHEELDOWN through __keyChord and write. Write = `lib.__keybindSet(command, slot, chord)`; status: ok and displacedUnbound -> KEY_UNBOUND_ERROR:format(GetBindingName(displaced)); ok -> KEY_BOUND; reason combat -> S.COMBAT; failed -> S.FAILED; then stop and repaint every row of this ctx. Stop: EnableKeyboard(false), EnableMouse(false), EnableMouseWheel(false), Hide, SetParent(UIParent), ClearAllPoints, restore the slot's text from GetBindingKey. Only one row listens at a time, across every host.
   - Capture stops on: the slot widget's OnRelease (ClearScroll on a tab change or a structural refresh), the page's OnHide (hook `ctx.panel` once per ctx, guarded by `ctx.__keybindHooked`; `ctx.panel` is the library's own panel, not a pooled widget), and the start of combat: a library-level combat hook `lib.__keybindOnCombat` held strongly on lib and registered in `lib.__combatHooks` (Options.lua:362; weak-keyed, so it must be held), replacing an older copy's hook on upgrade (`lib.__combatHooks[old] = nil`), which on `locked == true` stops any capture and writes S.COMBAT to that row's status. No new event registration for combat.
   - Every function CCN <= 15; the file stays < 1000 lines (split helpers; if it would pass ~900, stop and peel the capture listener into its own secondary file paired on the shell's minor, per CLAUDE.md 'A peel here is a release').

