REGISTRATION ROUTE (the CLAUDE.md register row `events-frames-taint-§1`, :77, lists three raw private registration sites and its re-check trigger is 'a fourth private registration site appears in LibKa0s/'): register through `core.SafeRegisterEvent(frame, "UPDATE_BINDINGS")` (Core.lua:481, the pcall'd helper the section asks for), so this is NOT a fourth raw site and the row does not fire. Unregister with the frame's UnregisterEvent. With no core.SafeRegisterEvent (an older vendored Core) do not register at all; the OnShow re-read and the refreshers still work. Add one sentence to that register row's Why cell noting that OptionsKeybinds registers through SafeRegisterEvent on purpose.

FILE LibKa0s/OptionsKeybinds.lua: KEYBINDS_MINOR 2 -> 3 (`Minor 3:` note).
- `lib.__keybindLive`: a weak-keyed set row-record -> ctx, added when a row is built, removed in the row group's OnRelease.
- `lib.__keybindEventFrame`: one hidden Frame created once, kept across upgrades; its OnEvent looks `lib.__OnKeybindEvent` up at call time (the OptionsCombat.lua:138-148 idiom), re-set on every load that gets this far.
- `lib.__syncKeybindEvents()`: drop dead rows; a row is on screen when its group frame answers IsVisible() (IsShown fallback, as OptionsCombat.lua:66-71); register UPDATE_BINDINGS when any is, unregister when none is. Called when a row is built, on its release, from the ctx.panel OnShow/OnHide hooks LK-12 installs (extend them), and at the start of each dispatch.
- `lib.__OnKeybindEvent(event)`: sync first; if nothing is on screen return having drawn nothing (a stand-down suite fires every event at every frame that ever owned one); else schedule ONE repaint: if `lib.__keybindRepaintPending` is set, return; else set it and `C_Timer.After(0, flush)` (no C_Timer: flush now). flush clears the flag and repaints every live, on-screen row (slots + set line) from GetBindingKey. A capture in progress is not interrupted by a repaint (the listening slot keeps S.LISTENING).
- OnShow re-read: the ctx.panel OnShow hook repaints that ctx's rows (fallback for a key changed while the page was hidden, as QuickComms did at db8f7a6:settings/Dials.lua:409-412). Repaints read only; they are allowed in combat.
- Every function CCN <= 15.

